The `15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s` condition (polymer_wt=15.0, bath_temp=9, pullcast_speed=6, mixing_temp=40, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=250, nips_bath_wait_time=1600, N2=true) has been run 10 times with highly variable results: pore fractions ranging from 0.50–0.85 and moduli from 198–315 bar. The mean pore fraction across clean runs is approximately 0.65–0.70, with occasional high outliers. The variability is substantial (run5 pore fraction 0.85 is likely an outlier given the top-gap defect and very low coupon humidity of 3.81%).

