### Decision

The `15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s` condition has been run 10 times already with high variability. Further repeats of this exact condition are not informative without understanding the source of variability. 

The `14-0add-8deg-N2-1250s` condition (polymer_wt=14, bath_temp=8, pullcast_speed=5, mixing_temp=30, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=120, nips_bath_wait_time=1250) has 4 runs with pore fractions 0.57–0.75 and moduli 103–246 bar. The mean pore fraction is ~0.67 and mean modulus ~177 bar — a reasonable Pareto position. However, the original run1 had the highest pore fraction (0.75) with the lowest modulus (103 bar), suggesting a fit quality issue.

