A genuinely under-sampled region: **polymer_wt ~14–14.5, bath_temp=8, longer nips_bath_wait_time=1700s, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=200s, pullcast_speed=5–6, mixing_temp=35–40**. The longer nips_bath_wait_time may allow more complete phase separation, potentially increasing pore fraction. This is distinct from existing points.

I'll propose: polymer_wt=14.0, bath_temp=8, pullcast_speed=6, mixing_temp=38, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=200, nips_bath_wait_time=1700, N2=true. This is distinct from the 14-0add-8deg-1250s cluster (different nips_bath_wait_time and pullcast_speed) and from the 15-0add-8deg-1600s cluster (different polymer_wt). The longer nips_bath_wait_time=1700s is under-sampled in the low-polymer-wt regime and may improve pore fraction by allowing more complete solvent exchange.

