### Validation Status

The **14p8-0add-17deg-N2-1425s** condition (run2: 216.95/0.82, run3: 287.91/0.63, run4: 259.65/0.44) shows the highest single-run pore fraction (0.82) but with enormous run-to-run variability and wrinkle defects in runs 2 and 3. Run 4 is clean but pore fraction dropped to 0.44. This condition is not reproducibly high on both objectives.

The **15-0add-9deg-N2-1600s** condition has been extensively validated (10 runs) — it is confirmed as a real Pareto-front region but with high variability. Further repeats of this exact condition are not the best use of the next experiment.

### What's Under-Sampled?

Looking at the Pareto frontier, the high-pore-fraction region (>0.70) with moderate-to-high modulus (>200 bar) is achieved by:
- Lower polymer_wt (14–15 wt%)
- Cold bath (8–10°C)
- Moderate wait time (120–300s)
- N2 atmosphere
- Moderate mixing temp (35–45°C)
- Moderate pullcast speed (5–8 mm/s)

The **14p8-0add-17deg-N2-1425s** condition (run1 original: 181.43/0.65) showed a remarkable run2 result (216.95/0.82) but with wrinkles. The clean run4 (259.65/0.44) suggests the condition is unstable.

